.TH MQ_RECEIVE 3 "July 2026" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
mq_receive, mq_timedreceive \- receive a message from a POSIX message queue
.SH LIBRARY
Realtime library (librt, \-lrt)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <mqueue.h>
.PP
.BI "ssize_t mq_receive(mqd_t " mqdes ", char *" msg_ptr ", size_t " msg_len ", unsigned *" msg_prio );
.br
.BI "ssize_t mq_timedreceive(mqd_t " mqdes ", char *" msg_ptr ", size_t " msg_len ,
.br
.BI "                        unsigned *" msg_prio ", const struct timespec *" abs_timeout );
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR mq_receive ()
removes the oldest message of the highest priority from the queue
.I mqdes
and copies it into the buffer
.IR msg_ptr .
The buffer length
.I msg_len
must be at least as large as the queue's
.I mq_msgsize
attribute (see
.BR mq_getattr (3)).
If
.I msg_prio
is not NULL, the priority of the received message is stored at
.RB * msg_prio .
.PP
If the queue is empty and
.B O_NONBLOCK
is not set for the descriptor,
.BR mq_receive ()
blocks until a message arrives or the call is interrupted by a signal.
.BR mq_timedreceive ()
behaves identically except that it blocks only until the absolute time
.RB * abs_timeout
(a
.B CLOCK_REALTIME
.BR "struct timespec" ),
after which it fails with
.BR ETIMEDOUT .
A NULL
.I abs_timeout
makes
.BR mq_timedreceive ()
block indefinitely, exactly like
.BR mq_receive ().
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success the number of bytes in the received message is returned.  On error
\-1 is returned and
.I errno
is set.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EAGAIN
The queue was empty and
.B O_NONBLOCK
was set for the descriptor.
.TP
.B EBADF
.I mqdes
is not a valid descriptor open for reading.
.TP
.B EINTR
The call was interrupted by a signal.
.TP
.B EMSGSIZE
.I msg_len
is less than the queue's
.I mq_msgsize
attribute.
.TP
.B ETIMEDOUT
.RB ( mq_timedreceive )
The queue remained empty until the timeout expired.
.TP
.B EIDRM
The queue was removed with
.BR mq_unlink (3)
while the call was blocked.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
char buf[64];
unsigned prio;
ssize_t n = mq_receive(q, buf, sizeof(buf), &prio);
if (n == \-1) perror("mq_receive");
else printf("got %zd bytes at priority %u\\n", n, prio);
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mq_send (3),
.BR mq_open (3),
.BR mq_getattr (3),
.BR mq_open (2)
